[42.328426, "o", ".6-35b — 15 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Now let me verify pip works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me do a quick sanity check that installing a package actually works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\npip is fully working again.\r\n\r\n**What was wrong:** Your Python 3.13 installation had a broken pip — the `pip3` script existed and the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory was present, but the actual `pip/` package files were missing from `site-packages`. This is a \"zombie install\" where metadata survived but the package was deleted or corrupted.\r\n\r\n**What I di"]
[42.328445, "o", "d:** Removed the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory, then ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip` which extracted the bundled `pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl` from `ensurepip/_bundled/` and installed it properly.\r\n\r\n**Result:** `pip3 --version` and `python3 -m pip --version` both report `pip 24.3.1` and a dry-run install of `requests` succeeds.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=18 surface=aac11e18eb0d\r\n"]
